[h1]Galaxy Generation Overhaul[/h1]

[b]Requires game to be launched via Mod Launcher[/b]

Take control of how your galaxy is built. This mod adds new options to the [b]New Game[/b] screen: real spiral arms, shape controls for every galaxy type, separate settings for how [i]many[/i] habitable planets there are and how [i]good[/i] they are, fairer empire placement, and optional full galaxy knowledge at the start.

[b]Most defaults reproduces the standard game[/b], so little changes until you touch a setting. Works with and without the Pirate Expansion.

[h2]Latest Release[/h2]
Version: {version} ({date})

[h2]Latest Changes[/h2]
{changes}

[h2]Galaxy shapes[/h2]
New rows appear in the galaxy settings step and change with the selected shape.

[b]Spiral[/b]
[list]
[*] Number of arms (2 to 7)
[*] Arm winding, arm width and arm taper
[*] Core size, center stars and field stars
[*] Rim thinning
[*] Nebula placement: inside the arms, or [b]between the arms[/b] (the new default)
[/list]

[b]Elliptical, Classic, Ring, Cluster and Irregular[/b]
[list]
[*] Elongation, concentration and bar
[*] Classic: nebula arms and nebula winding
[*] Ring galaxies: ring radius and ring stars
[*] Clusters: cluster amount, cluster size and variability
[*] Irregular: voids, web nodes, web strength and filament width
[/list]

The galaxy preview updates as you change the options.

[h2]Habitable planets[/h2]
The vanilla "Colony Prevalence" button is now the [b]frequency[/b] of habitable planets. A new [b]Planet Quality[/b] row controls how good they are, from very low to very high. Higher quality gives larger, richer populations. Lower quality leaves most worlds marginal.

[h2]Empire placement[/h2]
The vanilla search picks a random point and takes the nearest suitable planet. That can leave big areas empty and put an empire on a lonely star. The [b]Balanced regions[/b] option splits the populated part of the galaxy into one region per empire, each with about the same number of stars, and puts every empire in its own region. Your own start location setting (deep core, core, rim or a spot on the map) picks which region is yours. Choose [i]Standard[/i] for the original behaviour.

[h2]Galaxy knowledge[/h2]
Start with [b]Standard[/b] knowledge, [b]Explored[/b] (every system marked as explored) or [b]Surveyed[/b] (every planet, moon and asteroid surveyed, so all resources, bonuses and facilities are known without survey ships; ruins still need investigating). Available for standard empires and on the pirate empire screen.

[h2]Small galaxies[/h2]
Galaxies of 700 stars or fewer can use every galaxy size.

[h2]Pirate Expansion[/h2]
Compatible with the Pirate Faction and Lone Pirate start modes, and with Age of Shadows. Pirates are placed by the game's own logic, and the mod does not interfere with them. Without the expansion everything works as before.

[h2]Installation[/h2]
Subscribe, then enable the mod in the mod manager. Start a new game and open the galaxy settings.

[b]Notes[/b]
[list]
[*] Options apply to new games only. With DW2 Settings Keeper installed they are remembered between sessions; without it they return to their defaults when the game restarts.
[*] The same seed does not fully reproduce a galaxy in the base game, and that is still true with this mod.
[*] A log is written to [i]<Game Folder>data\Logs\SpiralArms.log[/i], which helps with bug reports.
[/list]
